      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A potential setup could involve a character mistakenly assuming a Mexican immigrant speaks no English or has limited language proficiency simply because of their accent or cultural background. The punchline could come when the immigrant responds to a question in flawless English, or when they order food and the cashier tries to skip to the problematic assumption. Alternatively, you could show the character asking the immigrant a series of elementary questions, like \"Do you speak Spanish?\" or \"Do tacos taste good?\", as if they're genuinely funny, when in reality, they're revealing their own limited knowledge. The contrast between the character's expectation and reality can be humorous.",
