      "content": "Here's an example:\n\n[Setting: A diner, with a character (think a pseudo-intellectual hipster type) sitting across from the Mexican immigrant]\n\nPseudo-Intellectual: \"I'm only having a burrito because I'm discovering the intricacies of Ac Celticification... you know, how dominant agricultural histories shape the cuisine of vassal nations.\"\n\nMexican Immigrant: \"Sir, I just had this delicious beef burrito because I love tacos.\"\n\nIn this example, the pseudo-intellectual tries to pass off a tired trope (Ac Celticification and classes dividing through food) in a smug way, while the immigrant calmly corrects him in a straightforward, honest manner, poking fun at the character's unnecessary convolutions and misplaced pretension.",
