      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's still kinda wordy and academic lol. the \"pseudo-intellectual\" thing is fine but it's not really hitting the \"satirizing the stereotype\" part because the actual joke is just a guy being weirdly smart. \n\nto make it actually bite, the character needs to be making a more \"obvious\" joke that everyone in the audience recognizes immediately—like something about them being loud, or always having family around, or something about the \"smell\" of certain foods. \n\ncan you try writing a version where the character makes a really blatant, stereotypical comment? don't worry about making the character \"smart\"—make them a bit of an idiot. just give me the dialogue where the joke is actually the stereotype itself, so i can see how to flip it in the script. like, just write the joke as it would be told by a clueless person.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
